# Station Lanes on the example rocket:
#   cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/lanes.drive /tmp/lanes
# Panel geometry at 1280x800: lanes y 558..764, ruler 558..582, lanes Structure 582, Aero 610, Propulsion 638 (two rows), Recovery 688, Avionics 716.
viewport 1280x800
move (640, 400)
screenshot rest.png
# Select the fin set: accent corner brackets, never a fill.
click (923, 624)
screenshot selected-fin.png
# Drag the ballast bar aft: both distances in the tag, mass shading, the tube's walls, CG and the margin follow live.
press (505, 730)
move (520, 730)
move (560, 730)
move (610, 730)
screenshot drag-mid.png
release (610, 730)
screenshot drag-done.png
# Hover a rail button: it is named with its station.
move (683, 624)
screenshot hover.png
# Hover the CG label: mass shading shows while the cursor is on it.
move (700, 758)
screenshot hover-cg.png
# Right-click empty space in the Recovery lane: only that system's parts, station prefilled.
click right(780, 702)
screenshot add-menu.png
# Choose one: it is added at that station (and selected).
click "Drogue"
screenshot added.png
# Drag a centering ring from the parts bin onto Structure: a dashed ghost in its own lane and the exact station on the ruler.
click (22, 149)
press (143, 224)
move (170, 240)
move (400, 420)
move (680, 590)
move (700, 596)
screenshot bin-drag.png
release (700, 596)
screenshot bin-drop.png
# The caret at the right end of the ruler (or L) collapses the lanes to the ruler.
click (964, 570)
screenshot collapsed.png
click (964, 752)
screenshot expanded.png
# Side-on (2D) view: the lanes lock to the viewport's scale, so every bar sits directly under the part it is.
click "2D"
move (640, 300)
screenshot locked-2d.png
# Resize: drag the aft end of the parachute bar.
press (672, 702)
move (685, 702)
move (705, 702)
screenshot resize-mid.png
release (705, 702)
screenshot resized.png
# Light theme.
click "Prefs"
click "Light"
click "Done"
screenshot light.png
